WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.450
Speaker 1: I want to start today with the
Haitian immigration crisis.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:14.369
This is potentially one of the first major
Joe Biden tests that is sort of going aimlessly

00:00:14.369 --> 00:00:18.310
and contributing to Joe Biden's declining
approval rating.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:25.230
We talked about Joe Biden needs a big accomplishment
to stem the decline in his approval rating.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.689
The situation with Haitian immigrants does
not seem to be helping.

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:31.390
So we're going to go through it.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:37.270
And I think, you know, it's there's this unfortunate
thing where every time I say, hey, guys, this

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.770
is Biden dropping the ball here, people angrily
email me and they say, David, have you become

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.469
some kind of right wing trump or whatever?

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:46.690
Presidents mishandle things.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.170
And it doesn't mean that I would prefer Donald
Trump to be president of the United States.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:56.260
Just sometimes presidents don't immediately
or at all handle situations correctly.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:00.500
And I think this is one of those situations
where due to its complexity and due to conflicting

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.879
messaging from the current administration,
it is hurting Joe Biden.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:07.159
And we can talk about to what degree that's
fair.

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:10.340
So let's start with some of the latest news
here.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.810
Reuters reporting angry scenes at Haiti airport.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.090
Add to Biden pressure over expulsions.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.790
And we'll talk about what that means in a
second.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:23.560
Angry scenes broke out at Haiti's main airport
on Tuesday among migrants sent home from a

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:28.940
squalid Texas border camp as U.S. President
Joe Biden faced mounting pressure to stop

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:34.400
an expulsions policy, the U.N. refugee refugee
chief said it may be illegal.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:40.180
Nearly 10000 migrants, mainly Haitian, remain
in worsening conditions in the impromptu camp

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.960
that sprung up under a bridge spanning the
as it's called in the in the U.S., the Rio

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.759
Grand from the Texas town Del Rio to Mexico
City.

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:50.950
That Akuna.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:55.470
In recent days, U.S. authorities have removed
at least 4000 people from the site for processing

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.369
and detention centers.

00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:02.140
Some five hundred twenty three Haitians have
been deported to their homeland on four flights,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.250
with repatriation set to continue on a regular
basis.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:10.070
According to DHS, returnees reacted angrily
as they stepped off flights at Port au Prince

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:14.310
airport after spending thousands of dollars
on arduous voyages from the troubled Caribbean

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:19.240
nation via South America, hoping for a better
life in the United States.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.550
On Tuesday, they found themselves back where
they started.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:25.790
A group of men in white T-shirts rushed back
toward the plane after they disembarked, with

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.340
one man attempting to get back on board.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.530
Witnesses said the migrants broke into a restricted
area of the airport as they attempted to recover

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:35.520
passports and personal belongings.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:41.040
Ground staff close the door of the plane before
the man could scale the steps back in.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:47.930
Tempers ran high, exacerbated by the news
the Haitian government had accepted the deportations.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:55.900
So there's there's an OK article in Politico
outlining the potentially problematic future

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.100
of this for Joe Biden.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:01.140
Now, before we look at the article, I think
it's important to mention part of the problem

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.780
here is that this is a very complicated situation.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:13.060
And you simultaneously have Jen Psaki saying
the treatment of the migrants is unacceptable

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.250
and you have deportations.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:19.560
But they're saying, well, the people being
deported are basically just the men, but the

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.880
women and children are staying and conservatives
are angry either way.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:30.060
So I'm not pretending that there is objectively
a correct solution here that would absolve

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.790
Joe Biden of any drag on his approval.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:38.490
But we can still acknowledge that this is
causing a problem for Joe Biden.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:44.820
The Politico article says Biden slips into
political quicksand amid Haitian migrant buildup.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.640
The articles by Natasha Korecki and Laura
Baron Lopez.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:53.790
And the article says the mass of thousands
of Haitians at the U.S. southern border has

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:58.770
put the Biden administration in the exact
place it's tried to avoid knee deep in immigration

00:03:58.770 --> 00:03:59.770
politics.

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:02.190
I think that's completely accurate.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:06.250
In the past 24 hours, the White House has
responded to images and videos of aggressive

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:11.490
tactics used by Border Patrol to corral migrants
by supporting an internal investigation into

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.620
the matter.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:16.930
What it hasn't done yet is figure out a solution
to the crowding and sanitary issues arising

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:21.950
in what's become a makeshift encampment or
stop its policy of deporting migrants upon

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:22.950
arrival.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:26.850
That's left the president and his team with
few supporters and allies.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:31.420
And we can talk about what should be done.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:36.510
While also recognizing that in terms of Biden
taking heat, there's almost really nothing

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.320
he could do right.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:42.950
You criticized the treatment of the migrants
by Border Patrol and the right says, oh, look,

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:48.630
you're on the side of the illegals rather
than have law enforcement and then you do

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.630
deportations.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:53.520
And the left says, well, but if we're acknowledging
that these people aren't being treated correctly,

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.810
then you just send them out back to the situation
that is a disaster in their country.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:02.410
Now, that's also bad and that's inhumane.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:06.540
And you don't improve the situation at the
encampment and that's inhumane.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:11.190
But if you do improve it, then the right says
you're coddling criminals as they like to

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.190
say.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:15.360
So I get that no matter what, there would
be criticism.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:20.560
And yet we can still talk about what is the
correct path forward, which we which we will

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.800
do.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.790
The article in Politico goes on to say, A
coalition of more than thirty eight civil

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:29.480
rights and immigrant advocacy leaders sent
the White House a letter calling on Biden

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:33.300
to stop expulsions, some of whom arrived to
the border community after fleeing violent

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:37.990
and natural violence and natural disaster
in their home country.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:44.550
The letter marks a final straw, said Nana
Gaddafi, executive director of the Black Alliance

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:50.990
for Just Immigration, described the moment
as an inflection point for Biden's commitment

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:54.710
to a humane immigration policy.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:58.430
Members of the president's own party, including
Chuck Chuck Schumer, echoed the call to end

00:05:58.430 --> 00:05:59.430
expulsions.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:03.410
Increasingly, they did so while directing
their ire at the White House for its handling

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:04.960
of the situation.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:10.890
Twelve House Dems will hold a press conference
calling on Biden to halt deportations.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:14.200
So what is it that should be done here?

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:19.031
It's not totally clear, but it's causing a
problem for Joe Biden, whose approval rating

00:06:19.031 --> 00:06:26.270
has now hit a new low of 43 percent as of
yesterday, Kamala Harris down to 49 percent.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:30.170
This is the lowest approval rating that Joe
Biden has had.

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:37.320
And this does not yet fully account for what's
going on at the border with the Haitian migrants.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:44.090
This poll ended on September 17th, and it
has Joe Biden down to a presidency low of

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.090
43 percent.

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:51.990
Now, it is typical that presidents see approval
decline throughout their presidency.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:55.430
As we've talked about before, many people,
just as soon as the president does one thing

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:58.950
they don't like, they say I no longer approve.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.040
And it's often difficult to change that.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:03.560
We've seen that with many presidents.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:09.480
At the same time, there is a question here
about whether Joe Biden drops into the 30s.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:14.070
And my expectation my prediction was, as we
saw the approval ratings start to go down

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:19.389
around the Afghanistan situation, which I
agree with, leaving Afghanistan is just as

00:07:19.389 --> 00:07:24.090
a reminder, if you've not seen those segments,
my thought was it'll get down into the low

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:27.550
40s before it might turn around and start
going up.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.780
I don't think the situation in Del Rio is
going to help.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.190
So what should happen?

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:42.560
You know, it seems as though a sort of balanced
approach here would be provide better conditions

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.919
and sanitation, figure out a way to do it.

00:07:44.919 --> 00:07:46.840
The right will say you're being soft.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.919
But remember, the right's been saying that
since January 22nd, before Joe Biden changed

00:07:51.919 --> 00:07:56.910
anything about what was being done at the
border, the right was already saying Joe Biden

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.660
is being soft.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:04.910
So either way, they're going to say that materially
improve the sanitation situation at the border

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:08.760
must do there's food shortages, et cetera.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:12.850
Do some kind of a temporary pause on the expulsions.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.590
Now, the right will say these people are here
illegally.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.260
So, of course, you're going to deport them.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:22.949
And at a certain point, this is going to have
to be adjudicated in a more serious way.

00:08:22.949 --> 00:08:27.650
But the problem is, if you don't put a pause
here, you don't even allow the opportunity

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:31.300
to say, is there a valid case for asylum here?

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.130
Now, many of us would say, obviously there
is.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.510
Look at the situation in Haiti.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.589
It's a legal question.

00:08:36.589 --> 00:08:40.510
But if you just immediately do the expulsions,
you don't even allow the opportunity to do

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:41.510
that.

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:42.510
You're not going to please the right.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:43.510
That's the reality.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:46.660
But at this point, nobody's happy with how
this is being handled.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:53.130
And I think the major criticism is it seems
aimless, where it's not really clear what

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.450
is even the goal down there.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:09:00.890
And so we will see if in the I think by Monday
there has to be some clear messaging and we

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:05.589
may even get it today from Jen Psaki, who's
going to be by the time you listen or watch

00:09:05.589 --> 00:10:05.350
today, the press briefing will likely already
have been held.

